msgid "Also consider that GROMACS and PLUMED will never delete your files. They will take backups when you try to overwrite them. GROMCAS backup files start with `#`, whereas PLUMED backup files start with `bck.`. Both GROMACS and PLUMED will complain if you try to create too many backups of the same file. It is thus recommended to regularly clean your directory with a command such as `rm -f \\#* bck.*`"
